","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4406795193,"indicator":"login.paypal.com.secure-verification.net","type":"hostname","created":"2026-06-11T16:31:57","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4406795194,"indicator":"vpn.company.com.secure-verification.net","type":"hostname","created":"2026-06-11T16:31:57","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["lookalike domains","domain impersonation","dns analysis","threat intelligence","brand spoofing","typosquatting","cognitive exploitation","phishing","social engineering","homograph attacks"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1583","T1071.004","T1204.002","T1566.002","T1598.003","T1071","T1586.002","T1583.001","T1589","T1589.002","T1584","T1586","T1598.002","T1204","T1590","T1566","T1598","T1590.001","T1204.001","T1584.001"],"references":["https:\/\/www.infoblox.com\/blog\/security\/human-judgment-hacks-how-lookalike-domains-work\/"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a2b2411d3d3323a465da4c0","name":"Affidavit in Support of Application for Criminal Complaint","description":"An FBI investigation identified Denis Nikolayevich Obrezko, a Russian national, as facilitating cyber intrusions conducted by the Russia-aligned threat group Void Blizzard. Between June and July 2024, multiple U.S. companies across various sectors were targeted in a large-scale cyber espionage campaign involving mass email harvesting and unauthorized access. The threat actors utilized stolen session tokens, proxy services, and VPNs to authenticate to victim Office 365 environments and exfiltrate data. Obrezko allegedly obtained critical infrastructure including a virtual private server and domain registration used in these attacks. FBI investigation linked Obrezko through cryptocurrency transactions, email accounts, phone numbers, and IP addresses to domains and infrastructure used in the intrusion campaign. Eleven U.S. companies have confirmed unauthorized access, representing only a fraction of suspected victims nationwide.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-06-15T19:15:30.295000","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:37.861000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"Void Blizzard","indicators":[{"id":1601732542,"indicator":"lnstagram.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:38","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4107862912,"indicator":"ebsummlt.eu","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:38","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4107862921,"indicator":"miscrsosoft.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:38","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4406889629,"indicator":"172.86.75.235","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:38","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-07-11T21:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4406889630,"indicator":"http:\/\/lnstagram.com\/wlsperrrrr\/","type":"URL","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:38","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4406889631,"indicator":"ffice365.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:38","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4406889632,"indicator":"micsroft.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:38","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["void blizzard","cryptocurrency","denis obrezko","proxy infrastructure","cyber espionage","russia-aligned","session token theft","office 365 compromise"],"targeted_countries":["United States of America"],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1133","T1114","T1071","T1562","T1567","T1589","T1185","T1090","T1020","T1588.001","T1070","T1586","T1590","T1048","T1588.002","T1566","T1078","T1573","T1598","T1213"],"references":["https:\/\/cyberscoop.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/3\/2026\/06\/11-1.pdf"],"industries":["Education","Finance","Technology","Government","Healthcare","Manufacturing","Retail","Energy"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a2b2414789fc7b619434890","name":"Defending the Digital Pitch: World Cup 2026 Cyber Threats","description":"The 2026 FIFA World Cup presents a concentrated attack surface spanning three nations, 16 cities, and billions of viewers. Cybercriminals have already launched phishing campaigns, fraudulent ticket sales, and brand impersonation schemes targeting governments, sponsors, broadcasters, transportation providers, and telecommunications companies. Financially motivated actors are exploiting tournament-related interest through credential theft and payment fraud. Hacktivist and state-aligned groups, including pro-Iranian actors like Handala and CyberAv3ngers, may conduct DDoS attacks, website defacements, or espionage operations amid heightened geopolitical tensions involving Iran, the United States, and Russia. Ransomware groups such as Qilin, DragonForce, Akira, and Play may target organizations reliant on continuous service availability. Thousands of FIFA-themed domains have been registered, many exhibiting characteristics associated with fraud campaigns. Organizations throughout the ecosystem face elevated ris...","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-06-15T19:10:01.751000","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:40.035000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4406889659,"indicator":"fifaticket2026vip.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:40","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["ddos attacks","credential theft","fifa world cup 2026","brand impersonation","ransomware","hacktivist","geopolitical tensions","phishing campaigns"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1557","T1583","T1539","T1566.002","T1190","T1583.001","T1589","T1185","T1588.001","T1586","T1528","T1204","T1199","T1566","T1110","T1078","T1499","T1598","T1189","T1498"],"references":["https:\/\/www.cyberproof.com\/blog\/defending-the-digital-pitch-world-cup-2026-cyber-threats\/"],"industries":["Government","Transportation","Telecommunications","Media","Hospitality","Finance"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a2b24146ff879b6eec74176","name":"World Cup 2026 Mobile Targeted Phishing: The Global Social Engineering Threat","description":"Threat intelligence has uncovered a significant increase in digital scams and phishing campaigns exploiting the FIFA World Cup 2026, specifically targeting mobile users. Three primary attack campaigns have been identified: The first uses typosquatting and institutional spoofing with fake domains like fifa-tickets[.]vip to deceive ticket buyers. The second mimics major sports retailers such as Nike and Adidas, hiding infrastructure behind Cloudflare to steal payment credentials. The third campaign, dubbed OffsideHire, exploits tournament hiring through sophisticated recruitment fraud using an Adversary-in-the-Middle platform targeting corporate Google Workspace accounts with real-time MFA bypass capabilities. These campaigns leverage emotional urgency, ticket scarcity, and mobile device usage patterns to bypass traditional security controls, posing risks to both individuals and enterprise environments through credential harvesting and session hijacking.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-06-15T19:08:50.962000","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:40.488000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4380308769,"indicator":"fifa-tickets.vip","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:41","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4384157356,"indicator":"fifa-hiring.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:41","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4384157357,"indicator":"fifa-hr.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:41","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4406889642,"indicator":"ec7b0bc82c00464d8e0a59bc19c585e2","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:41","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4406889643,"indicator":"fifa-careerpath.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:41","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4406889644,"indicator":"fifajobs.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:41","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["credential harvesting","typosquatting","mobile targeting","social engineering","google workspace","world cup 2026","aitm","phishing"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1539","T1114","T1566.002","T1598.003","T1566.001","T1586.002","T1608.001","T1583.001","T1589","T1185","T1056.003","T1589.002","T1608.005","T1528","T1566","T1056","T1589.001","T1598","T1204.001"],"references":["https:\/\/zimperium.com\/blog\/world-cup-2026-mobile-targeted-phishing-the-global-social-engineering-threat?hs_amp=true"],"industries":["Retail","Hospitality","Technology"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a2b24138a34132bc69a0072","name":"Targets Education Sector with Oracle PeopleSoft Exploit","description":"Between May 27 and June 9, 2026, UNC6240 (ShinyHunters) conducted an active compromise and extortion campaign targeting Oracle PeopleSoft application infrastructure. The threat actor exploited CVE-2026-35273, a critical remote code execution vulnerability (CVSS 9.8) in the Environment Management component, as a zero-day before Oracle's June 10, 2026 advisory. Over 100 organizations were potentially affected, with 68 percent operating in higher education and most based in the United States. Attackers deployed customized MeshCentral agents masquerading as Microsoft Azure services, established C2 infrastructure at azurenetfiles.net, and used lateral movement scripts to propagate across internal networks. The campaign culminated in data exfiltration and publication of stolen data on the ShinyHunters Data Leak Site on June 9, 2026. Compromised systems received defacement markers and extortion notices.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-06-15T19:02:52.797000","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:39.327000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"UNC6240","indicators":[{"id":4383395550,"indicator":"http:\/\/azurenetfiles.net:443\/agent.ashx","type":"URL","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:40","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4383395551,"indicator":"azurenetfiles.net","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:40","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4405629436,"indicator":"CVE-2026-35273","type":"CVE","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:40","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4406846002,"indicator":"176.120.22.24","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:40","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-07-11T21:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4406846008,"indicator":"c7e9332731b06644fc73e0046a2a89eaa59b09f54250e9bd622467187351711f","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:40","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4406889648,"indicator":"ebcf977806f68af3147e0b78b55f6aed","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:40","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4406889649,"indicator":"cc19e502e4201cc974c753b96429027925224f53","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:40","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4406889650,"indicator":"2ab684d93c1553fad87041b4dea97188a97e78589deee2a7bacff905564f3a35","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:40","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4406889651,"indicator":"68257a6f9ff196179ec03624e849927f26599eb180a7c82e14ef5bc4e93bc309","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:40","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4406889652,"indicator":"d83fdb9e53c5ff03c4cb0451ea1bebd79b53f29eadc1e2fa394c7af13a86ce2f","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:40","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4406889653,"indicator":"f02a924c9ff92a8780ce812511341182c6b509d45bc59f3f7b522e37225d24fc","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-11T21:09:40","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["higher education","data extortion","oracle peoplesoft","shinyhunters","lateral movement","zero-day exploitation","meshcentral","cve-2026-35273","unc6240"],"targeted_countries":["United States of America"],"malware_families":["MeshCentral"],"attack_ids":["T1560.001","T1110.001","T1133","T1069","T1114","T1036.005","T1021.004","T1190","T1491","T1505.003","T1083","T1552.001","T1041","T1059.004","T1078","T1027","T1486","T1573.002","T1071.001","T1018"],"references":["https:\/\/cloud.google.com\/blog\/topics\/threat-intelligence\/shinyhunters-targets-education-sector-oracle-exploit"],"industries":["Education"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a2c3a96a7d09d029d6f4a35","name":"UNC1151\/Ghostwriter phishing campaign targeting Gmail accounts","description":"The UNC1151\/Ghostwriter group is conducting high-intensity phishing campaigns targeting Gmail accounts of Polish citizens since March 2026. The campaigns primarily target individuals in political and public life, prominent positions, researchers, journalists, public administration and law enforcement employees, and their associates. Attackers use fraudulent emails impersonating Gmail administrators, claiming suspicious activity or policy violations to pressure victims into verifying their accounts. The phishing infrastructure captures login credentials and two-factor authentication codes through fake login panels. The group utilizes dedicated domains, Netlify subdomains, and compromised websites to host phishing pages. Campaigns run primarily on weekdays with new domains appearing almost daily, demonstrating persistent operational tempo against Polish targets.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-06-15T18:44:52.799000","created":"2026-06-12T16:57:58.097000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"Ghostwriter","indicators":[{"id":4316329224,"indicator":"mailverify.digital","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-12T16:57:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4345535064,"indicator":"check-mail-verify.biz","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-12T16:57:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4360663080,"indicator":"verify-check.digital","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-12T16:57:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["unc1151","gmail","phishing","poland","2fa bypass","credential theft","apt","ghostwriter"],"targeted_countries":["Poland"],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":[],"references":["https:\/\/cert.pl\/en\/posts\/2026\/06\/UNC1151-gmail-campaign\/"],"industries":["Government","Media"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a2c3a96b8b55a7623148b35","name":"How to defend ARM64 cloud infrastructure","description":"ITScape (CVE-2026-46316) is a guest-to-host escape vulnerability in the vGIC-ITS emulation within KVM\/arm64, disclosed by researcher Hyunwoo Kim. The flaw stems from a race condition in the vgic_its_invalidate_cache() function causing a double-put use-after-free, enabling host kernel code execution. Since the bug exists in in-kernel KVM rather than QEMU user-space, successful exploitation grants host kernel privileges, posing significant risk to multi-tenant ARM64 cloud environments. The vulnerability can be chained with local privilege escalation when guest root access is unavailable. Affected kernels range from commit 8201d1028caa through 13031fb6b835, when the patch was applied. Two YARA rules have been developed for detection: one targeting hardcoded constants from the proof-of-concept, another identifying behavioral patterns in privilege drop sequences.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-06-15T18:42:03.404000","created":"2026-06-12T16:57:58.756000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4402240066,"indicator":"CVE-2026-46316","type":"CVE","created":"2026-06-12T16:57:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4408469184,"indicator":"e0ab84da2d2783c8cae3624e8ce58b99ad79219753b249671ff7f743abdacc35","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-12T16:57:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4408469185,"indicator":"838ea8d6b201e2eed181f3fd890f99ecb6178b52","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-06-12T16:57:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4408469186,"indicator":"fbf0b6abd651622864eb921f891b3e7c538fc8a9","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-06-12T16:57:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["itscape","yara rules","arm64","cloud infrastructure","cve-2026-46316","kvm","guest-to-host escape","vgic-its"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1592","T1082","T1005","T1611","T1610","T1548","T1059","T1609"